{"actions":[{"actionCode":"H19000","actionDate":"2025-06-10","source":"House committee actions","text":"Ordered to be Reported in the Nature of a Substitute by the Yeas and Nays: 15 - 13.","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":"H15001","actionDate":"2025-06-10","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-01-03","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"Intro-H","actionDate":"2025-01-03","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1000","actionDate":"2025-01-03","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/59","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"O000175","fullName":"Rep. Ogles, Andrew [R-TN-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TN"},{"bioguideId":"R000614","fullName":"Rep. Roy, Chip [R-TX-21]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-01-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-16T18:39:26+00:00","id":"hr59-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-03","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-06-10","text":"Ordered to be Reported in the Nature of a Substitute by the Yeas and Nays: 15 - 13."},"laws":[],"number":"59","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"B001302","district":5,"fullName":"Rep. Biggs, Andy [R-AZ-5]","party":"R","state":"AZ"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-03","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Mens Rea Reform Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill establishes a default <em>mens rea</em> standard (i.e., state of mind requirement) for federal criminal offenses—statutory and regulatory—that lack an explicit standard.</p><p>The government must generally prove that a defendant acted knowingly with respect to each element of an offense for which the text does not specify a state of mind.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>","updateDate":"2025-02-11T22:10:02Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Mens Rea Reform Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-05-27T14:20:28Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-05-27T14:20:28Z"}
